    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Adjudication — judgement, when the mechanism ran out of facts",
      "prov:value": "## Why this exists\n\nOwner, 2026-09-21: *\"during review process a concensus/mechanical agreemenet\nwas not reached, in this case Judgment is needed and Adjudication process\nbeing … it is Judgment of >= 1 Feedback Provider's feedback. still have same\ndispensation process (reason for choice as per contextual requirements).\"*\n\n**The shape was already implemented seven times and generalised none.**\nMeasured 2026-09-22 over `processes/*.bpmn` and `src/`:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this exists",
      "prov:value": "The first two are the same sentence twice, written by different hands about\ndifferent subjects. The last two are an HTTP route and a schema that share no\ncode with the diagrams and arrived at the diagrams' rule anyway.\n\n**\"Named nowhere\" would be the easy summary and it is wrong.** It is named\nonce — `translation-workflow.bpmn`'s `Lane_Reviewer` documentation states the\nentry condition, the accountability and the dispensation rule together:\n\n> *\"a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles. The word is used here because\n> the passage reaching this lane is one where a checker and a translator\n> disagree, and somebody has to choose between them WITH a reason. That reason\n> is the record, not the choice.\"*\n\nWhich is the whole skill, in one lane's documentation, in one diagram, reachable\nonly by somebody already reading that diagram. **The gap was never vocabulary.\nIt was that nothing generalised the one statement of it**, so each new subject\nrestated it and the eighth would have restated it again."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this exists",
      "prov:value": "## One judgement, six questions — and the split that followed\n\n**Measured 2026-09-23** (bean `bvuk`, [#1073](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/1073)), and it changes how you call this process.\n\n`adjudication.bpmn` used to hold two things: the judgement, and three outcomes\ndone about it — the finding stands, the criterion is scoped, a dispensation is\ngranted. Six diagrams called it. **Only two asked a question those three\nanswer**: the `review-narrative` and `voice-review` rows above. The other four\nask whether a drift is real, whether a passage is acceptable, whether two\nentries agree, and *which side wins a conflict*. None of those has a criterion\nto scope or a dispensation to grant — and a `callActivity` runs the whole\nsubprocess, so all four ran the outcome half anyway.\n\n**Two things worth carrying, because both were established by checking rather\nthan reasoning:**\n\n- **No caller branched on the outcome, and none could.** Every one of the six\n  call activities has exactly one outgoing flow, and the process had one\n  settled end event: all three branches reconverged on `A_RecordEntry`. So the\n  mismatch was invisible in the callers' shape — a diagram asking \"which side\n  wins\" and one asking \"does this finding stand\" looked identical.\n- **Passing each caller its own codes could not fix it.** That was the first\n  proposal. The codes selected three different TASKS, so a caller handed\n  `local-wins` would have had it pointing at `A_ScopeCriterion`. **The branches\n  had to move, not the enum.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean bvuk",
        "#1073",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "One judgement, six questions — and the split that followed",
      "prov:value": "spec-kit's adjudicated status by the same codes | the answer moves a requirement SET's stage (issue #2405, FR-013) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2405",
        "FR-013"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "One judgement, six questions — and the split that followed",
      "prov:value": "`GW_SignoffRecorded` then reads\nthe record BACK through `decisions/requirement-signoff-recorded.dmn`, with facts\n`check:requirements --signoff-facts <reqset:slug>` computes from the store, so a\nsign-off nobody recorded loops back rather than proceeding (SC-008).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "SC-008"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What that means when you call it",
      "prov:value": "- **Declaring nothing** is legal and **reported** by `check:workflow-refs` —\n  the four callers above are in that state on purpose. What each should ask is\n  open, and guessing would make an undecided thing look checked."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What that means when you call it",
      "prov:value": "**a judgement\nnobody wrote down is indistinguishable from a checker that was never run.** It\nis `relaxable=\"false\"` wherever it lands, which is now with the caller that\nrecords, because the entry written depends on what was adjudicated."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The dispensation is a VERSION, never a precedent",
      "prov:value": "`A_Dispensation` is marked `relaxable=\"false\"` — in\n**`criterion-adjudication.bpmn`**, with `A_RecordEntry`, since the 2026-09-23\nsplit; this paragraph said `adjudication.bpmn` until 2026-09-24, four sections\nafter §\"One judgement, six questions\" had already recorded the move. **The\njudgement is free and the record is not**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23",
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Who adjudicates — a skill that spreads, an entitlement that does not",
      "prov:value": "**Plural by design**: the owner's *\"Judgment of >= 1 Feedback Provider's feedback\"*. |\n| `adjudicator` (role) | settles it, with a reason."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Who adjudicates — a skill that spreads, an entitlement that does not",
      "prov:value": "`translation-adjudicator` is the first specialisation and was the only\nadjudicator role before this skill existed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/adjudication.md#provenance-11",
